Qwen3.8-Flash-Next / Qwen4-Exp architecture (PR #36497) patch-application step
for container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly.

Adds one COPY+RUN step that applies sglang-qwen4exp-pr36497.patch (upstream
PR #36497 — the ONLY implementation of Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration /
model_type qwen4_exp, which exists in no tagged release and not in main) to the
sglang Python source AFTER the SM121 sgl-kernel patches but BEFORE
`uv pip install ./python`, so the installed package picks up the new model.
Same pattern as dockerfile-qwen36-mixed-nvfp4.patch.

Apply to: container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly AFTER dockerfile-sm121.patch
has been applied. Application is gated by build_sm121_image.sh on the recipe
variable APPLY_QWEN4EXP_PR36497=1 (set in sglang-0.5.18-sm121.recipe; remove the
variable / set 0 once PR #36497 is merged into the pinned SGLANG_REF —
re-applying a merged patch fails the in-container dry-run and aborts the build).

STACKABLE: like dockerfile-qwen36-mixed-nvfp4.patch this hunk uses ONLY trailing
context (the `# Install sglang package` comment block) with no leading context,
so it inserts immediately before that comment regardless of whether another
model patch (dsv4, qwen36) already inserted its COPY+RUN block there first.
build_sm121_image.sh applies this as step 2h, after 2c (dsv4) and 2f (qwen36),
so on a recipe with several of them enabled this block ends up last, directly
before `# Install sglang`. Works standalone too.

NOTE the runtime half: this build step does NOT carry the SM121 QSA decode
fixes. Those live in roles/k8s_dgx/files/sglang_patches/p65_qsa_sm121_sparse_
decode.py and are applied at container start, deliberately — one of the two is
a DEFENSIVE veto that must survive image re-bumps, see that file's docstring.
An image built from this step alone crashes at backend init on GB10.

FIXED 2026-08-28: the hunk header said `+293,19` while the body is 18 added plus
3 context lines = 21. GNU patch stopped after 19 and aborted with "malformed
patch at line 53", which means `patch --dry-run` in build_sm121_image.sh would
have die()d on every build with APPLY_QWEN4EXP_PR36497=1. Latent, not observed:
sglang-0.5.18-sm121.recipe (the only recipe setting that flag) has never been
built. Count corrected to 21, nothing else touched; re-verified by applying
dockerfile-sm121 -> this -> dockerfile-nemotron35-spec onto a pristine
container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly.

--- a/container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly
+++ b/container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly
@@ -293,3 +293,21 @@
+# Qwen3.8-Flash-Next / Qwen4-Exp architecture (upstream PR #36497, not yet
+# merged; captured from the upstream-owned branch qwen4-main-squashed @
+# 99c9362e). 94 files, 52 of them new: the qwen4_exp model + its MTP head +
+# config classes, the Qwen Sparse Attention (QSA) backend and kernel package,
+# the arch registrations in arg_groups/overrides.py, and small hooks into the
+# hybrid linear-attn / speculative / memory-pool machinery. Applied to the
+# sglang Python source before pip install so the installed dist-packages picks
+# up the changes. This COPY+RUN step only exists in builds whose recipe sets
+# APPLY_QWEN4EXP_PR36497=1 (the dockerfile patch adding this step is gated by
+# build_sm121_image.sh).
+COPY patches/sglang-qwen4exp-pr36497.patch /tmp/sglang-qwen4exp-pr36497.patch
+RUN set -e; cd /data/sglang && \
+    echo "=== Applying sglang-qwen4exp-pr36497.patch (PR #36497) ===" && \
+    patch --dry-run -p1 < /tmp/sglang-qwen4exp-pr36497.patch && \
+    patch -p1 < /tmp/sglang-qwen4exp-pr36497.patch && \
+    grep -q 'class Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration' python/sglang/srt/models/qwen4_exp.py && \
+    echo 'Qwen4-Exp PR #36497 patch applied successfully'
+
 # Install sglang package (no deps, no build isolation since base has torch).
 # Moved here from its original early-stage location so the installed
 # dist-packages picks up the patched nvfp4_blockwise_moe.cuh above.
